course: dictionary
lesson: 6471
title: NATO: a name, a promise and a code
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: NATO is written in capitals because it is a short form of a longer name: North Atlantic Treaty Organization. It is an alliance, which means a group of countries that agree to work together. «NATO is a military alliance of 32 countries in Europe and North America» tells you where its members are.
explain: The most important idea is a promise. «NATO members promise that an attack on one counts as an attack on all.» If one member is attacked, the others agree to help defend it. You can find this meaning by reading the words around NATO.
explain: NATO can also mean something else: the NATO alphabet, a list of code words for letters such as Alpha, Bravo and Charlie. Pilots and police use it so that letters are not mixed up on the radio. Check the sentence to see which meaning is being used.
fact: NATO stands for North Atlantic Treaty Organization.
fact: NATO is an alliance: a group of countries that promise to defend each other if one of them is attacked.
fact: «NATO is a military alliance of 32 countries in Europe and North America», and Finland joined in 2023 and Sweden in 2024.
fact: The NATO alphabet gives each letter a code word, such as Alpha for A, Bravo for B and Charlie for C.
fact: In the UK it is sometimes written as Nato, but capitals are the usual way to write it.
exercise: What do the letters in NATO stand for? | *North Atlantic Treaty Organization | North African Trade Office | Nordic Army Team Outpost | National Air Transport Operations
exercise: «NATO members promise that an attack on one counts as an attack on all.» What does this promise mean? | Members can never leave their homes | Members only trade bananas | *If one member is attacked, the others will help defend it | Members must attack any country that is close to them
exercise: On the radio, which NATO code word stands for the letter B? | Delta | *Bravo | Alpha | Charlie
test: «Finland joined NATO in 2023 and Sweden in 2024.» Which year did Sweden join? | *2024 | 2023 | 2022 | 2025
test: In the NATO alphabet, which code word stands for the letter C? | Echo | Alpha | *Charlie | Bravo
exam: Which sentence best describes NATO? | *A group of North American and European countries that promise to defend each other | A dance from Italy | A type of weather | A kind of bread from Spain
